course: dictionary
lesson: 10645
title: Unimportant and what matters
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unimportant means not important, not mattering much. Look at its parts: un- means not, and important means it matters a lot. So unimportant is the opposite of important.
explain: «Pupils learn to pick out the important facts and ignore unimportant ones.» In a maths problem that asks how far a car went, its colour is unimportant. Ask yourself: does this detail help me answer the question? If not, you can leave it out.
explain: «Being ignored, pushed or interrupted makes them feel unimportant.» The clues are ignored, pushed and interrupted, which are all unkind. So unimportant here means feeling as if you do not matter. Try your meaning in the sentence: "makes them feel not mattering". It still makes sense.
fact: Unimportant means not important; not mattering much.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unimportant is the opposite of important.
fact: «Unimportant details» are facts you can leave out of a summary.
fact: «Seem unimportant» means look as if they do not matter, though they may still be useful.
fact: «It doesn't matter a bit» means the same as unimportant.
exercise: In a maths problem, the colour of the car is unimportant if the question asks how far it went. What does unimportant mean here? | Very large and heavy | *Does not matter much for the answer | Painted bright red | Hard to read
exercise: «Some jurors write «important» and some «unimportant»; Alice thinks «it doesn't matter a bit».» What does Alice think? | That she needs more time | *That the choice does not matter at all | That the choice is very important | That the answer is a secret
exercise: «Some parents are glued to their phones, and it can make children feel unimportant.» How might a child feel? | As if they are very tall | As if they are a famous star | As if they have won a prize | *As if they do not matter much
test: Which detail is unimportant when a question asks how many apples were sold? | How many apples were sold | The total money earned | The price of one apple | *The colour of the basket they were in
test: «Being ignored makes a child feel unimportant.» Which phrase is closest in meaning to unimportant? | Very famous | *Not mattering much | Wide awake | Extremely clever
exam: Which word means the opposite of unimportant? | Small | Careless | Calm | *Important
